+## Session S61 (fix C) — BB-SLP: nested promoted sub-word SELECT demotion (2026-09-21)
+
+**Commit `8c5814b`** on `work` (base `c160d11`). Snapshot
+`S02-s61-slp-nested-subword-demote` — `ms178-1.patch` 234 393 B, sha256
+`80343d0b…d63cc4`, applies clean. Full write-up:
+`engineering/FOLLOWUP-2026-09-21C-slp-nested-subword-demote.md`.
+
+**Defect**: the sub-word SELECT demotion handled one level of promoted clamp.
+A two-sided clamp promotes the whole tree, so the outer arm is itself a
+promoted SELECT and shape extraction rejected it before any pack was built —
+`clamp_u8x16` sat at 161 scalar `cmov` instructions against clang's 5, gap 204
+of the probe's total 480.
+
+**Fix, four parts** (`src/passes/slp_vectorizer.rs`, +485/−43):
+(C1) `build_demoted_select_arm`, a recursive arm demotion reusing every
+soundness primitive of the top-level path, accepting **both** compare
+spellings — the temporary form keeps the inner compare promoted, the
+single-expression form has it narrowed at lane width; (C2) `strip_arm`
+normalizes a nested arm (bare `Select`, or a truncation around one) to the
+bare inner `Select`; (C3) `strip_copies` + copy transparency in `build_pack`,
+which had no `Copy` recognizer at all; (C4) `Copy` joins the retire
+fixpoint's feeder kinds — **the actual blocker**, a legality rule (a)
+rejection caused by the copy the front end emits for a twice-read temporary,
+invisible in both the IR dump and the assembly.
+
+**Red-team finding closed**: `packed_int_minmax` mapped unsigned 16/32-bit
+lanes onto `vpmaxsw`/`vpmaxsd` (signed). Not reachable from C — promotion
+delivers unsigned compares as `Ugt`/`Ult`, which the min/max spelling table
+rejects — but hardened to fail closed and pinned by a test that asserts both
+directions.
+
+**Results** (`-O2 -march=x86-64-v3`): `clamp_u8x16` 161→**33**,
+`clamp_u16x8` 86→**31**, `clamp_i16x8` 96→**22**, `clamp_i8x16`→**27**,
+`clamp3_i32x4` (3 levels)→**23**, all branch-free and vectorized.
+**lccc now beats gcc -O2 on all six straight-line clamps** (78/72/62/52/42/32).
+Probe gap **480 → 304**, entirely `clamp_u8x16`, **no other function moved**.
+Runtime `clamp_u8` **51.25×** faster, `clamp_i32` **12.64×**; checksum
+identical across lccc-before/after and gcc-O2/O3.
+
+**Gate defect found in my own test**: the previous
+`check_bb_slp_nested_ifconv.sh` ran `awk` over function names absent from the
+file under test, got an empty body, and read that as "zero branches" —
+silently satisfying a *must-branch* contract. Two of five contracts were
+checking names that did not exist. Rewritten so a missing symbol is a hard
+failure; self-tested by substituting a bogus name (exits 1).
+
+**Method note**: three consecutive diagnoses were wrong and each was
+plausible. What settled it was instrumenting the decision points instead of
+reasoning from the assembly — six tagged bail sites, a gate trace, per-arm
+results, and a per-`return None` trace over `build_plan`. The blocking
+condition left no trace in any dump.
+
+**Next**: `abs_i16` 17.86× behind gcc-O2 (needs a packed-abs intrinsic,
+`pabsw`); `VecMaxU32x8`/`VecMinU32x8` via SSE4.1 `pmaxud`/`pminud` to recover
+the fold closed above; `same_source` still `Copy`-blind.
